# 8. Water-Level Sensor — 1 Unit

The water-level sensor monitors the amount of water available in the irrigation storage tank.

### Why it was selected

Monitoring soil moisture alone is not sufficient for intelligent irrigation.

The system must also know whether sufficient water is available.

The water-level measurement therefore provides information about the system's available water resource.

This becomes particularly important for the **water-budgeting functionality** of AgriGuard.

For example:

```text
Tank Water Available
          +
Zone Water Requirements
          +
Zone Priority
          ↓
Water Allocation
          ↓
Irrigation Decision
```

The water-level sensor therefore connects the physical water supply with the irrigation decision-making system.

