# 10. Pull-Up Resistors — 4 Units

Four resistors are used as pull-up resistors for digital input signals.

These are associated with the physical control inputs such as the system switches and safety controls.

### Why pull-up resistors are required

A digital input can become **floating** when a switch is open and no defined voltage is applied to the input.

A floating input can produce unpredictable HIGH and LOW readings.

A pull-up resistor establishes a defined default HIGH state.

When the switch is activated, the input can then be pulled LOW.

Conceptually:

```text
VCC
 │
[Pull-up resistor]
 │
 ├──────── ESP32 GPIO
 │
 Switch
 │
GND
```

This produces a stable digital input and improves the reliability of the switch and safety-control circuitry.

